course: dictionary
lesson: 10343
title: One word, many meanings: transformer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one a writer means. Look at the words around the word. «Near your town, transformers in a humming substation turn the voltage down so it is safe enough to use in homes.» The clues are voltage, substation and homes, so a transformer here is a piece of electrical equipment.
explain: Now read this: «A transformer has two coils of wire round an iron core and changes the voltage, up for long lines and down for homes.» The clue is changes the voltage. Ask yourself: what does this thing do? That question often reveals the meaning.
explain: The same word can also name a toy. Transformers is a famous toy and film series about robots that change into cars and trucks. Context tells you whether the writer means the power station or the robot.
fact: A transformer is a device that changes the voltage of electricity, making it higher or lower.
fact: Power stations send electricity long distances at high voltage, and transformers lower it before it reaches homes.
fact: Substations hum because the iron inside a transformer vibrates.
fact: Anything that changes something else can be called a transformer.
fact: In computing, a transformer is a type of computer program used in many modern AI language models.
exercise: «Near your town, transformers in a humming substation turn the voltage down.» What does turn the voltage down mean? | *Make the electricity weaker so it is safe for homes | Make the robots fall over | Make the toy quieter | Switch off the town lights for ever
exercise: What is a step-down transformer? | A robot toy that turns into a truck | A computer program for AI | Something that makes the voltage higher for long lines | *A device that lowers the voltage so electricity is safe for homes
exercise: Which meaning of transformer fits a film about robots that change into cars? | A device that changes the voltage | *A robot that changes into a car or truck | A computer program used in AI | A coil of wire round an iron core
test: «A transformer has two coils of wire round an iron core and changes the voltage.» What does the sentence say a transformer changes? | *The voltage | Its size | Its colour | Its name
test: Why does a substation hum? | Because the wind blows through it | *Because the iron inside vibrates | Because the robots are talking | Because children are singing nearby
exam: Read: «Transformers is a famous toy and film series, but at the substation transformers turn the voltage down.» What does transformers mean in each part? | Both mean robot toys | Electrical devices in the first part, robot toys in the second | Both mean electricity | *Robot toys in the first part, electrical devices in the second
